  "final_answer": "Based on an audit of the Angular frontend (`ui-ngx`), modifying or deleting the backend endpoint `POST /api/apiKey/*PARAM*/rotate` is **SAFE** and will have **no impact** on the frontend application.\n\n### Key Findings:\n1. **No References Found**: There are no references to the endpoint `/api/apiKey/.../rotate` anywhere in the Angular codebase.\n2. **API Key Service Analysis**:\n   The central frontend service handling API keys, `ApiKeyService` (`ui-ngx/src/app/core/http/api-key.service.ts`), only communicates with the following endpoints:\n   - `POST /api/apiKey` (Save/Create API Key)\n   - `DELETE /api/apiKey/${id}` (Delete API Key)\n   - `PUT /api/apiKey/${id}/description` (Update Description)\n   - `PUT /api/apiKey/${id}/enabled/${enabledValue}` (Enable/Disable API Key)\n   - `GET /api/apiKeys/${userId}` (Fetch API Keys)\n\n### Conclusion:\nSince the frontend does not invoke or rely on the `rotate` endpoint, any refactoring, modification, or deletion of `POST /api/apiKey/*PARAM*/rotate` is **SAFE** and does not constitute a breaking change for the Angular application.",
